Once the service receives a LogPurchase call from the remoting runtime, it puts the
message in the LogQueue to avoid the caller remaining blocked, waiting for message
processing completion. This way, we achieve both the reliability of a synchronous message
passing protocol (the caller knows that the message has been received) and the
performance advantages of asynchronous message processing that are typical of
asynchronous communication.
